    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.35,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"extra_component\",\n      \"components\": [\"R4\", \"R5\", \"R6\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"REG1.24\", \"REG1.31\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"REG_FB\", \"+5V\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"On the Power sheet, R4 (19k6) runs from the +5V node (the C6/C7 and L1 output node) to the REG_FB net. R5 (6k8) also runs from +5V to the feedback node, and R6 (1k3) runs from that node to GND. R4 therefore sits in parallel with the top leg of the feedback divider.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The feedback divider should be R5 (top) and R6 (bottom) only, as the schematic note 'Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)' states. With R5=6k8 and R6=1k3 that gives about 5 V. Paralleling R4 changes the top resistance to about 5.05 k\u03a9 and would give a Vout of roughly 3.9 V, not 5 V.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"Power sheet (page 1): R4 19k6 between +5V node and REG_FB; R5 6k8 and R6 1k3 forming the divider; note 'Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)'\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Main buck regulator (5 V rail) ... notes \\\"L = 15uH for 5% ripple current\\\", \\\"Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)\\\"\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If R4 is not intended, the 5 V rail regulates to a lower voltage than designed, which can starve the servo and 3V3 LDO supply and cause brown-outs or unreliable operation.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.35\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_value\",\n      \"components\": [\"REG_PWM_PCA9685\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U2.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"+3.3V\"],\n      \"observed\": \"On the FCC Peripherals sheet, the PCA9685PW address pin A0 (pin 1) is tied to +3.3V, while A1 to A5 are tied to GND. The sheet note reads 'I2C address: 0x41'.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The specification lists the PWM driver at I2C address 0x40, which requires A0 to be tied to GND (all address pins low).\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"FCC Peripherals sheet (page 5): PCA9685PW pin A0 labelled +3.3V; note 'I2C address: 0x41'\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The FCC will address the PWM driver at 0x41 rather than 0x40. Firmware expecting 0x40 gets no acknowledge, so servo outputs would not be driven.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The drawing shows a feedback resistor (R4 19k6) in parallel with the 5 V regulator's top feedback resistor, which contradicts the stated Vout formula and would shift the output away from 5 V. A second, lower-confidence discrepancy is that the PCA9685 has A0 tied high, giving address 0x41 instead of the specified 0x40.\"\n}",
